Z||000000||Bluebottlejunky||05-26-2001||11:30 PM||||Well today was a long and sad day, took Fiero into shop to get inlet to muffler welded..45 min later."we cant weld it sorry, we will have to get all new exhaust system in price $400"  So I say no..and that is it..  When he brings it out of the shop garage the gears scraping and you can hear him pullin really hard on the shifer..he stalls the car.im so mad.  I tell him Ill take the car from there..and about 4 miles from home I notice I have no 1st or 3rd.  So I creap home sad, mad, and pissed.  I get home pop the deck lid and notice that the aluminum plate that the shifting linkage is broke on one side..and no clip holding it in. Well that is my trouble. (like to thank Scott Lafortan SP of the Wisconsin Fiero Fanatics) So that needs to be fixed, and I took off my exhaust so I can order a new one from fiero store.  And that is my sad day..I will never trust a mechanic agian.  <BR>PS Anyone got one of those aluminum plates that the shifting linkage slides into and has the clips that pop into it to hold it all? Im so tired right now..I hope y'all dont get to confused by my grammer. THANKS<P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||8
